  <h2 class="mt-0">Across the hill from Gedling</h2>
  <p>Gedling village and Carlton are on the eastern side of the borough, with Arnold over the ridge to the north-west. It's a short drive, and for many owners Arnold is on the way to work anyway. Daycare drop-off is around 7:30am and collection around 5pm.</p>
  <p>Paws 2 Purrs is licensed by Gedling Borough Council, which looks after Gedling, Carlton and Netherfield too, and fully insured. Vanessa has 10 years' experience caring for other people's dogs.</p>

  <h2>Owners here know a good walk</h2>
  <p>Gedling Country Park, on the old colliery site, has given this side of the borough some of the best dog walking around, with woodland, ponds and big open views. Carlton owners have Colwick Country Park and the lakes a short way south. Dogs from this side of town are used to proper walks.</p>
  <p>They get just that with Vanessa's pack: woods, farm fields and water spots, ball play on the way, and most dogs off lead or on a long line. She'll explain where the pack goes at your meet &amp; greet.</p>

  <h2>Pick what you need</h2>
  <ul>
    <li><strong>Long working days?</strong> <a href="/dog-daycare-arnold-nottingham/">Doggy daycare</a> gives your dog company and exercise instead of a long day alone.</li>
    <li><strong>Holidays and weekends away?</strong> <a href="/dog-boarding-arnold-nottingham/">Licensed home boarding near Gedling</a>: sofas, their usual sleeping spot and a large enclosed garden. <a href="/christmas-dog-boarding-nottingham/">Christmas</a> spaces are limited.</li>
    <li><strong>Midday walks?</strong> <a href="/dog-walking-arnold-nottingham/">Walks with pick-up and drop-off</a>, plus dog pop-ins.</li>
    <li><strong>Cat at home?</strong> <a href="/cat-sitting-arnold-nottingham/">Cat pop-ins</a> and small animal feeds.</li>
  </ul>

  <h2>Huskies especially welcome</h2>
  <p>There's no size limit at Paws 2 Purrs, and huskies are Vanessa's favourites. One owner of "a boisterous husky" described her as "a proper dog whisperer". Small dogs are just as welcome.</p>
